D405 Seam Tracking experimental framework: original wrappers, contracts, wall geometry,
fusion, evaluation, CLI and passive ROS adapter. No third-party repository was vendored.

Direct runtime use: NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), OpenCV (Apache-2.0), PyYAML (MIT),
installed tank-vision-inspection async_lifecycle (local project dependency).
Training: segmentation_models.pytorch 0.5.0 (MIT, per-file exceptions retained in wheel),
PyTorch 2.5.1 and torchvision 0.20.1 (BSD), timm 1.0.15 (Apache-2.0),
ONNX 1.17.0 (Apache-2.0), ONNX Runtime 1.20.1 (MIT).
Offline wheels retain their original dist-info license and notice files.
No pretrained model or weight is downloaded or supplied as a seam model.

RealSense ROS 4.57.7 and installed librealsense 2.58.4 (Apache-2.0) are existing
device owners and factory-calibration sources, not copied into this project.
Projection equivalence uses OpenCV Brown/fisheye APIs and tested pixel contracts.
Unknown/inverse-Brown distortion is rejected, never guessed.

D-Robotics rdk_model_zoo rdk_s (Apache-2.0) and installed local S100 examples
were consulted for API usage. The native adapter is newly written against the
installed proprietary DNN/UCP headers; SDK libraries/headers are NOT redistributed.
No NV12 sample code, model asset, classification output or zero-copy claim is reused.

robotic-sealing (license not found at reviewed commit), seam_detection (GPL-3.0),
and DFormer are method/research references only. No source, dependency or model
from these three projects is included in the first deployment.
Exact versions, commits, local SDK hashes and verification status appear in
README.md and reports/framework_validation.json.
